  body: "# Deferring State Pension entitlement\n\n## Source-backed proposal\n\nThe captured SP guidance calls postponement
    or suspension of entitlement deferral and says that this regime has no own-deferral lump-sum option of the kind
    described for RP.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThis is the person’s own SP deferral; inherited deferred RP
    and survivor options are separate provisions. Days excluded from increments, overseas residence, notices, claims
    and cited memos require review. No advice about whether an individual should defer is given.\n\n## Inspected
    passages\n\n- [DMG 74501, PDF page 58](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f255d3e08b8871b665ab/dmg-Ch-74.pdf#page=58).\n\
    - [DMG 74526, PDF page 62](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f255d3e08b8871b665ab/dmg-Ch-74.pdf#page=62).\n\
    \n## Provenance and review\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of DWP guidance, not an official DWP document.
    All definitions and relationships are model-assisted and unreviewed. No individual eligibility, award, legal
    conclusion or executable rule is supplied.\n\nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, stated
    legal date and pension event date have separate meanings. PDF page numbers are one-based file positions; extraction
    may damage reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n-
    `dmg-vol12-ch74` — PDF SHA-256 `5961a9cb7c86814a0f6fa147c0a8a551b4258c803680fac14a95cab9eca1afd6`; page-extraction
    SHA-256 `c762e93940b4342d70d5bc96a80c3e094c91852d93868f5709e04f293faef61a`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/sp-entitlement-suspension
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source includes opting to suspend entitlement within the definition of SP deferral.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol12-ch74/0062
      quote: "74526 A person’s entitlement to SP is deferred for a period if they\n\n\n1. opted1 to suspend their
        entitlement for that period 2 or\n\n\n2. are not entitled to SP for that period only because\n\n\n     \
        \ 2.1 they have not made a claim3 or\n\n\n      2.2 they have deferred their entitlement to any other SP4.\n\
        \n\nNote: This also applies5 to overseas residents (see DMG 74574 et seq).\n\n\n                       \
        \                     1 Pensions Act 14, s 16; 2 s 17(7); 3 s 17(8)(a); SS Admin Act, s 1;\n           \
        \                                           4 Pensions Act 14, s 17(8)(b) & (9); 5 s 17(7) & (8) & 18"
      locator: DMG 74526
  - target: term/rp-deferral-election
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source explicitly contrasts the SP deferral route with RP increments/lump-sum options; no
      equivalence of the two regimes is asserted.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol12-ch74/0058
      quote: "74501 [See Memo ADM 09-25] [See Memo DMG 01/26] Entitlement to SP starts on the day all the\nconditions
        for\n\n\n1. pensionable age and\n\n\n2. contributions and\n\n\n3. claims\n\n\nare satisfied. However, people
        may postpone or suspend 1 their entitlement to SP. This is known as\ndeferral. For RP purposes people may
        be able to choose Incs or a lump sum payment. However, for SP\npurposes there is no lump sum payment option.\n\
        \n\n                                                                                   1 Pensions Act 14,
        s 16"
      locator: DMG 74501
